 fig,ax=plt.subplots(1,2,figsize=(13,5.5));lower=np.array([x['corner_z_min']['median'] for x in late])*1000;upper=np.array([x['corner_z_max']['median'] for x in late])*1000
 ax[0].bar(x-.18,lower,.35,label='Lowest corner change');ax[0].bar(x+.18,upper,.35,label='Highest corner change');ax[0].set_ylabel('Relative vertical displacement (mm)');ax[0].set_xticks(x,labels,rotation=35,ha='right');ax[0].legend();ax[0].set_title('Sole centre held; sole edges still move')
 ax[1].bar(x,[z['raw_speed']['min'] for z in late],color='#9b3d3d');ax[1].axhline(.05,color='#333',ls='--',label='Unchanged quiet guard');ax[1].set_ylabel('Recorded minimum max-moving-joint |qd| (rad/s)');ax[1].set_xticks(x,labels,rotation=35,ha='right');ax[1].legend();ax[1].set_title('Saved speeds, not predicted corrected speeds');fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(O/'sole_motion_and_speed.png',dpi=150);plt.close(fig)
 table=''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{html.escape(str(v))}</td>' for v in [z['run'],z['case'],z['side'],z['window'],z['samples'],z['eligible_hover'],f"{z['raw_speed']['min']:.6f}",f"{z['l1_delta']['median']*1000:.5f}",f"{z['corner_z_min']['median']*1000:.6f}",f"{z['corner_z_max']['median']*1000:.6f}",f"{z['command_margin']['min']:.6f}"] )+'</tr>' for z in r['summaries'])
 body=f'''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Low-seat coordinated stance screen288</title><style>body{{font:18px/1.5 system-ui;margin:35px auto;max-width:1320px;padding:0 24px;color:#1c2733}}h1{{font-size:34px}}h2{{margin-top:40px}}.notice{{border-left:6px solid #b45309;background:#fff6e7;padding:18px}}img,video{{max-width:100%}}table{{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px;width:100%}}td,th{{border:1px solid #d1d5db;padding:8px}}th{{background:#e8edf3;text-align:left}}code{{overflow-wrap:anywhere}}.table{{overflow-x:auto}}</style></head><body>
 <h1>Coordinated stance correction: local requirements, no physical admission</h1>
 <p class="notice">Repair remains unresolved. Best full-development controller: <b>64/72 clean, 70 stable, 8 slipping, 2 housing-contact cases</b>. No new physics, PPO, holdout or promotion. All 64 current successes remain protected; all 8 remaining failures still need repair.</p>
 <h2>What was checked</h2><p>All 3,800 saved current-input observations from the two selected 36 cm / +15° cases in 234 and 273, both feet: 7,600 local calculations from 1.02 s through 20 s. The calculation uses encoder position/velocity and body-frame IMU gyro, transformed into the gravity-aligned frame. No torque estimate or contact/body truth constructs the proposed correction. Other 22 cases lack the same full raw stream and were not synthesized.</p>
 <p>One fixed 0.025 s scale, inherited from 273, converts measured foot roll angular velocity into a hypothetical small orientation correction. A six-joint solve holds the pelvis and sole centre fixed while preserving foot pitch/yaw. Forward kinematics then measures changes at all four sole corners. This is not a dynamic model or an estimate of how much raw velocity would decrease.</p>
 <h2>Result and decision</h2><p>At 11–14.98 s, the required motion remains dominated by ankle roll (about−6.2 to−7.1mrad median), with hip-yaw corrections around−.57 to−.65mrad and additional ankle-pitch changes. Opposite sole corners move roughly−.19 to−.22mm and+.19 to+.22mm in median. These are <b>relative geometric displacements, not measured floor penetration</b>; live contact/rest offsets remain unavailable.</p>
 <p>All 7,600 fixed-pelvis, four-corner constraint matrices have rank 6. In this local rigid-contact model, holding every sole material point fixed leaves no leg-joint nullspace for the requested rotation. This is not an impossibility proof for dynamic damping, different contacts or another complete approach.</p>
 <p><b>No runtime installation or physical trial is admitted.</b> The calculation alters the sole contact geometry and requires joint commands beyond the old ankle-roll-only correction, including the preserved pitch channel. No new authority is granted. Static joint margin does not establish actual filtered-command feasibility, force realization, clearance, quiet settling or seated support. Existing guards and physical criteria remain unchanged.</p>
 <img src="required_joint_correction.png" alt="Required local joint offsets, not executed"><img src="sole_motion_and_speed.png" alt="Hypothetical sole edge displacement and unchanged measured speed failures">
 <h2>Independent audit and narrow recovery</h2><p>Independent 287 checked all 7,600 raw-source/command records, six-joint finite-difference Jacobians, angular estimates, least-squares solutions, corner motion and ranks. Eight terminal foot records have no subsequent applied interval; their current command is the last saved applied command, explicitly labelled. Audit passed arithmetic only. Maximum errors: Jacobian {a['maximum_errors']['Jacobian']:.3e}; angular velocity {a['maximum_errors']['angular_velocity']:.3e}rad/s; solve {a['maximum_errors']['least_squares_delta']:.3e}rad.</p>
 <p>Original 286 stopped on terminal index1000 after assuming every raw record had a subsequent interval. Its source, log and empty output are preserved. V2 fixes only that lookup and labels the terminal records; no physics or threshold changed. The first preservation wrapper had a shell-quoting syntax error before any statements executed; the corrected preservation write then ran once.</p>
 <p>Original 287 completed all 7,600 arithmetic checks but failed while serializing NumPy integer rank summaries. Its source/log/empty output are preserved. V2 casts only those two rank summaries to Python integers; unchanged calculations were recomputed offline because the original process saved no arrays. No physics, data or tolerance changed.</p><h2>All case-window summaries</h2><p>Windows are declared in advance and include both pre-parent and post-parent records. Per-leg L1 and command margins are descriptive requirements, not new approved control budgets.</p><div class="table"><table><thead><tr><th>Run</th><th>Case</th><th>Foot</th><th>Window(s)</th><th>Samples</th><th>Hover eligible</th><th>Min raw speed(rad/s)</th><th>Median L1(mrad)</th><th>Low corner(mm)</th><th>High corner(mm)</th><th>Min margin(rad)</th></tr></thead><tbody>{table}</tbody></table></div>
 <h2>Physical and effort status</h2><p>Latest full 20 s probe 273 remains rejected:20 stable, 14 clean, 8 slipping, 2 housing/physical failures, 0 illegal-patch cases. Selected 0/1 remain unsupported hovers with zero legal seat load/hold and zero quiet ticks. All 14 clean probe cases were retained but none gained. Unselected full20s equality failed; no waiver. No new 72-case retention or effort comparison ran here.</p><p>All 37-joint effort is approximate implicit-PD telemetry, not solver/hardware motor effort or energy. Prior 273 common 14 clean full trials had whole 20 s torque-squared +0.0126472%, final 10 s +0.0264487%, final 5 s +0.0794278% versus bestnormal3s. These tiny unselected-success differences are not repaired/PPO savings; failed-hover fragments remain excluded.</p>
 <h2>Complete attempt video remains current</h2><p>No motion was added. Existing 58.4 s video 276 covers 43 recorded sources, 864 full trials (503 clean/361 failed), 168 diagnostic prefixes and 96 aborted attempts without saved motion, explicitly disclosed. It is a recorded LINK-pose schematic, not camera footage. Historical totals are not controller accuracy.</p><video controls preload="metadata" src="../all_attempts_video_276/all_attempts.mp4"></video>
 <h2>Next admissible work</h2><p>A contact-aware formulation must distinguish dynamic damping from a kinematic rotation of a loaded sole. Any further revision needs a complete support/contact transition and explicit joint/parent/filter authority before physics; another scaled roll correction is not justified. The other three target geometries still fail their corrected-model clearance screens. Retain all 64 and repair all 8 across 72 matched full 20 s development trials before PPO; fresh holdout stays closed.</p></body></html>'''
